# =============================================================
# Research materials — what is and isn't safe to commit
# =============================================================
#
# THE RULE: anything that reproduces a publisher's text stays local.
# Anything we wrote ourselves is tracked.
#
# NOT COMMITTED — copyrighted source material:
#   * the retrieved PDFs themselves
#   * every derived extraction of them: source.md, candidates/,
#     figures/, tables/, manifest.json
#
# An extraction is still the publisher's words, just reformatted.
# Machine-converting a paywalled paper to markdown does not make it
# ours to redistribute, and two of these were obtained through
# institutional access. Same status as the PDF.
#
# COMMITTED — our own work:
#   * research/FETCH-RESULTS.md
#     (provenance record: source URLs so anyone with equivalent
#     access can re-fetch the set — no publisher text)
#   * the literature review, synthesis, and notes we write
#   * short quotations under fair dealing, properly attributed
#
# -------------------------------------------------------------
# Papers and their extraction packages
# -------------------------------------------------------------
research/papers/
research/extracted/
research/.cache/

# Extraction artifacts, wherever they end up
*.pdf
**/candidates/
**/manifest.json
**/*.direct.md
**/*.ocr.md

# -------------------------------------------------------------
# Explicitly tracked (guard against the patterns above)
# -------------------------------------------------------------
!research/*.md
!research/notes/
!research/notes/**

# =============================================================
# OS / editor noise
# =============================================================
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vs/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# =============================================================
# Unity
# =============================================================
# Generated, machine-specific, or rebuildable from Assets/ +
# ProjectSettings/ + Packages/manifest.json. Those three ARE tracked.
[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
[Mm]emoryCaptures/
[Rr]ecordings/

# Never tracked: Unity regenerates these and they hold absolute local paths
/[Aa]ssets/AssetStoreTools*
/[Aa]ssets/Plugins/Editor/JetBrains*
.consulo/
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.tmp
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# Unity3D generated crash reports
sysinfo.txt

# Builds
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.app

# Crashlytics
crashlytics-build.properties

# Addressables
/[Aa]ssets/[Aa]ddressable[Aa]ssets[Dd]ata/*/*.bin*
/[Ss]treaming[Aa]ssets/aa.meta
/[Ss]treaming[Aa]ssets/aa/*

# =============================================================
# Simulation output
# =============================================================
# Evolutionary runs produce large archives and logs. Genomes worth
# keeping get promoted into a tracked champions/ directory by hand.
runs/
!runs/.gitkeep
*.jsonl

# Spike measurement output. Raw CSVs are regenerable, so they're ignored —
# but FINDINGS.md is the record of what was measured and DESIGN.md §11.1
# links to it, so it stays tracked.
spikes/**/results/*.csv
